<p>Great news everyone! With the help of the amazing <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/bibliolatry" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3534136); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3534136&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1552780371" alt="bibliolatry" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3534136)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/bibliolatry" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3534136); return false;">bibliolatry</a></span>, a minecraft map based around Site-M1 has been created and is now available for download!</p>
<p>Some things I need to state:</p>
<ul>
<li>The map was designed within Minecraft: Java Edition. We are not sure if it will work in any other version, such as bedrock edition or pocket edition.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Lag warning for the chambers themselves: don't expect perfect performance, especially if your system isn't that great.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>If you want to preview the map without downloading it/or if you don't own minecraft, here's an <a href="https://imgur.com/a/0J5InH5">imgur album</a> showing multiple parts of the map.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Many, many easter eggs.</li>
