<p>It's a very believable, well-made map. Nice work <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/bibliolatry" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3534136); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3534136&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1571962819" alt="bibliolatry" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3534136)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/bibliolatry" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3534136); return false;">bibliolatry</a></span>!<br />
Nice use of chickens instead of a mob grinder, definitely fits better space-wise and doesn't rely on lighting up the whole map. Using shulker boxes to carry documentation and emergency supplies was likewise smart.</p>
<p>That said, I'm not sure the MKA makes a lot of sense: if a random person stumbles onto this, they're given docs on the basics of what to do and a phone number to call. Would killing them really be that productive, they're facing off against a cognitohazard anyways.</p>
<p>Also I think it would be worthwhile to terraform the area right around the entrance to make it match the screenshot.</p>

